```
Reason:
The use of `compareAndSet` on the `AtomicBoolean initialized` allows multiple threads to enter the block where `initialized(context)` is called before the initialization is complete. If one thread calls `matches` and sets `initialized` to true, another thread could still enter this block and call `initialized(context)` again, leading to unexpected errors due to incomplete initialization.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
if (!this.initialized) {
    synchronized (this.initializeLock) {
        if (!this.initialized) {
